# Confirm before every git push

The user wants to personally authorize every push (the usual Cursor / GitHub "authorize push to master" step).

- Never run `git push` (or any command that updates a remote) until the user has just confirmed in this conversation that they are ready to authorize that push.
- "Commit and push" or "update cloudflare" is not enough. After the commit, stop and ask them to confirm the push so they can click authorize.
- Do not use stored git credentials to push silently in the background.
- After they confirm, then push and wait for their authorize prompt.
